{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-tags-page-tsx","path":"/blog/tags/reverse-engineering/","result":{"data":{"tags":{"group":[{"fieldValue":"adventofcode","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"binary analysis","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"fuzzing","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"ghidra","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"linux","totalCount":3},{"fieldValue":"papers","totalCount":5},{"fieldValue":"pharos","totalCount":3},{"fieldValue":"programming","totalCount":4},{"fieldValue":"prolog","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"publications","totalCount":4},{"fieldValue":"quick thoughts","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"research","totalCount":6},{"fieldValue":"reverse engineering","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"rust","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"skiing","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"talks","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"travel","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"ubuntu","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"web","totalCount":3}]},"posts":{"totalCount":2,"edges":[{"node":{"htmlAst":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I was playing around with "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://chat.openai.com/share/89f6e196-ea09-48f9-b64c-ca0084ac9a90"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"ChatGPT"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and it came up with this gem:"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"blockquote","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the thrilling world of ones and zeros, where the mere thought of assembly code sends shivers down the spines of mere mortals, there exists a unique breed of masochists—reverse engineers. Are you the kind of person who looks at a complex problem and thinks, \"Why not make it harder?\" If the idea of disassembling convoluted code into something even remotely understandable without any upfront instructions sounds like a fun Tuesday afternoon, then we have the perfect job for you."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"blockquote","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Introducing the glamorous world of reverse engineering, where the nightmares of dealing with assembly code, hexadecimal hellscapes, and cryptic comments—or the lack thereof—don't just haunt you in your sleep; they're your 9 to 5. Ever wanted to spend hours, nay, days, unraveling the mysteries of code that was never meant to be understood, like an archeologist deciphering the Rosetta Stone, except what you're translating doesn't want to be translated? Congratulations, your masochistic tendencies can finally pay off."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"blockquote","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In this role, you will dive headfirst into the abyss of other people's code, armed with nothing but your wits and perhaps an unhealthy dose of caffeine. You'll experience the unparalleled joy of finally understanding a function's purpose at 3 AM, only to realize it was a decoy. But fear not, for the fruits of your labor are many—aside from the occasional existential crisis. You'll gain the satisfaction of knowing you're outsmarting attempts to keep you out, one painstaking line at a time."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"blockquote","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"So, if you're someone who relishes the thought of your brain being tied into knots by assembly language, who finds the idea of decrypting software protections better than a crossword puzzle on a Sunday morning, and who sees a \"No Trespassing\" sign as a personal invitation, then the lucrative world of reverse engineering awaits. Where else can you get paid for indulging in your penchant for digital masochism? Join us, and turn your nightmares into your day job."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ready to sign up? 🤣"}]}],"data":{"quirksMode":false}},"timeToRead":1,"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2024-02-26--in-the-thrilling-world-of-ones-and-zeros/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["reverse engineering"],"title":"In the thrilling world of ones and zeros...","updatedDate":"26 February, 2024","image":null,"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","bio":"Computer Security Researcher","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/83fe9/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/83fe9/ed.png 35w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/ad998/ed.png 70w","sizes":"35px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/dbb7e/ed.webp 35w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/299bc/ed.webp 70w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"35px"}]},"width":35,"height":35}}}}}}},{"node":{"htmlAst":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"My colleagues and I finished the camera ready version of our "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"/papers/ase19.pdf"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"DIRE"}]},{"type":"text","value":" paper on "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"/blog/2019-08-17--august-2019-updates/"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"variable name recovery"}]},{"type":"text","value":".\nAlthough there's no code released at this time, I'm hoping to release a proof of\nconcept Hex-Rays plugin."}]}],"data":{"quirksMode":false}},"timeToRead":1,"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2019-09-22--dire-camera-ready-available/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["research","reverse engineering","papers"],"title":"DIRE ASE 2019 Camera Ready Available","updatedDate":"01 April, 2020","image":null,"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","bio":"Computer Security Researcher","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/83fe9/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/83fe9/ed.png 35w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/ad998/ed.png 70w","sizes":"35px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/dbb7e/ed.webp 35w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/299bc/ed.webp 70w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"35px"}]},"width":35,"height":35}}}}}}}]}},"pageContext":{"tag":"reverse engineering"}},"staticQueryHashes":[],"slicesMap":{}}